US Census Bureau — TIGER/Line and Geocoder
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

School district, city, county and ZIP boundaries, and address-range geocoding, are
derived from US Census Bureau TIGER/Line products and the Census Geocoder.

  https://www.census.gov/programs-surveys/geography.html

US Government works are in the public domain (17 U.S.C. §105). No attribution is
required. It is given because naming the source of a boundary is useful to the
reader, not because a license compels it.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FEMA — National Flood Hazard Layer
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Flood zone determinations are derived from the FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer.

  https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps/national-flood-hazard-layer

Public domain. No attribution required; given for the same reason as the Census
entry above. FEMA flood zone data is informational and is not a substitute for an
official flood determination.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Google Places
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Where points of interest are supplied by the Google Places API, they are subject
to the Google Maps Platform Terms of Service rather than to an open data license.

  https://cloud.google.com/maps-platform/terms

Google's terms govern caching and display separately from the open-data sources
above: Place content is not persisted beyond what those terms permit, and the
provenance record for a Google-sourced row carries the place_id reference only.
